+# ECON-02B2d18c — Cosmetic color and safe generic factory placement (partial d18c)
+
+Date: 2026-11-01. Exact baseline: ECON-02B2d18b source archive, SHA-256 `43eb0cf545ae2019403808ce26d6e4140da86fbe8cd4fd507a28639d028506d9`.
+
+## Shipped locally
+
+- **White-default, eight-color outpost paint:** `white`, `slate`, `sand`, `red`, `blue`, `green`, `yellow`, `violet`. Single color per existing outpost, shown in its colony construction plan map. The selected style is saved in a new `sg_site_appearance` SQLite table; no material debits, new resources, or changes to physics snapshots. This is cosmetic metadata: the colored map is real but a 3D building shader is NOT implemented. Per-building variation, patterns, decals, and material customization are deferred.
+- **Authorization:** GET `/factory/api/color?site=` and POST `/factory/api/site_color` use the existing localhost token/origin checks and are dispatched through the same C++ colony writer thread. The native controller binds site/ship/owner to the session and allows only the eight canonical palette identifiers. Cross-site, forged token, forged origin, invalid color and restart tests are included.
+- **Real grid placement safeguards for the existing approved generic factory:** Installing a generic machine is rejected if its footprint crosses installed legacy equipment or a built wall/door inside that footprint. A generic conveyor cannot overlap positioned existing equipment or cross a built structural edge. Building a new wall/door is rejected if it cuts through an installed generic machine or generic conveyor path. Placing legacy equipment atop installed generic infrastructure is also rejected. Rejection occurs before any module debit.
+- **No fabricated inventory:** Existing site ownership, module custody, production, and SQLite resource journaling remain unchanged. Existing two-machine template (100/200) and conveyor (800) still use the same canonical world writer.
+
+## Verified evidence
+
+- Complete Linux Ninja/CMake native build: **passed**.
+- CTest: **113/113 registered tests individually passed**, in disjoint runs: **78 standard tests**, **24 completed of 35 live/relay tests** before the execution window ended, then the **11 unfinished live/relay tests passed** in an isolated run. Do not describe the first live run as a successful 35-case invocation.
+- JavaScript suite: **93/93 passed**.
+- Offline Chromium colony structures, crew, and generic factory controls: **3/3 passed**. Mocked browser transport verifies UI behavior, not native HTTP authorization; dedicated native HTTP tests cover real protocol and SQLite behavior.
+- New d18c real-HTTP spatial test: verifies built wall prevents machine installation, installed machine prevents an interior wall, installed conveyor prevents a wall across its path, and denied installation does not consume modules.
+- Existing d18b generic factory real-HTTP and d5 structure authorization/SQLite restart HTTP tests pass.
+
+## Explicit non-completion
+
+This milestone closes only **color palette + bounded physical placement checks** of ECON-02B2d18c. It does NOT implement per-building painting, 3D materials, pattern editor, NPC-carried material transfer to generic machines, expanded machine catalogs, generic worker schedule integration, grid-based utility hookups, or Windows GUI acceptance. A future integration milestone must address remaining generic-factory custody and staffing gates. GitHub is a repository only; these changes were built/tested locally and are not pushed.
